    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rovjbi9",
      "content": "The Takin (Budorcas taxicolor) is the State Animal of Arunachal Pradesh. It is a massive bovid found in the bamboo forests of the Eastern Himalayas, including Tawang and West Kameng districts."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a29dp51",
      "content": "The Great Hornbill (Buceros bicornis) is the State Bird. It holds great cultural significance for many tribes; the Nyishi traditionally used its beak in their Bopia headgear, which has now been replaced by fibreglass replicas to protect the species."
    },
