      "content": "Namdapha National Park — Key Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Namdapha National Park is frequently tested regarding its unique location, ecosystem, and species diversity.",
        "Eagle Nest Wildlife Sanctuary is a high-yield topic for questions on bird sanctuaries and endemic species.",
        "Be prepared for match-the-following questions pairing forest types with specific flora and fauna highlights."
      ],
      "id": "kvnayqj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lzb6wmm",
      "content": "Namdapha is one of India's most biodiverse national parks and is the third largest in the country. It is the only park in the world where all four felid species of big cats — tiger, leopard, clouded leopard, and snow leopard — coexist. It is also a part of the Indo-Burma biodiversity hotspot and has exceptional bird diversity with over 400 species recorded."
    },
    {
      "id": "wdmh6pc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Eagle Nest Wildlife Sanctuary — Birding Paradise"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hq86inq",
      "content": "Eagle Nest WLS in West Kameng district is widely regarded as one of the best bird-watching sites in the world. It is famous for the discovery of the Bugun Liocichla (Liocichla bugunorum), a new bird species discovered as late as 2006. The sanctuary hosts over 450 bird species and attracts birdwatchers from across the globe."
    }
